{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"422a615dcce2626e87c735bd3cf9079cf3e60583db92d9a4fa7c3aba1697cd60","digest":{"component_or_area":"GitHub Actions metrics adapter","key_entities":["src/rebar/metrics/adapters/github_actions.py","scripts/harvest_gha.py","tests/unit/metrics/test_gha_adapter.py",".rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson","src/rebar/metrics/snapshot.py","src/rebar/metrics/registry.py","src/rebar/metrics/__init__.py",".github/workflows/test.yml","pytest-cov TOTAL line"],"problem_keywords":["GitHub Actions","coverage harvest","CI health","metrics persistence","log retention","snapshot storage"],"propositions":["An optional isolated GHA adapter must parse coverage percentage from pytest-cov TOTAL line in run-log tail and extract CI-health (status, duration, red-to-green recovery, flake rate) from run-metadata JSON.","Coverage and CI-health snapshots must be persisted to the git-tracked .rebar/metrics-snapshots.ndjson store via the harvester script, not via CI workflow changes, to preserve durability beyond GHA's retention window.","The GHA adapter must be isolated from core metrics modules (registry.py, __init__.py) and future _commands/metrics.py so no adapter imports appear in those files.","The harvester script harvest_gha.py must pull recent test.yml run logs and metadata via gh/Actions API and append labeled snapshots to the tracked store without modifying the CI workflow."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787546100335531001,"uuid":"9381a261-9206-47b1-9954-a91443a24985"}